4. **Big Green Egg** - Perfect for smaller gatherings or camping trips, the MiniMax Big Green Egg is a compact yet mighty ceramic grill. With only 133 sq. in. of cooking space, this little guy packs a punch when it comes to delivering premium performance. And at just over 30 lbs., transportation has never been easier!
5. **Traeger** - Looking for a state-of-the-art wood pellet grill with advanced technology? Look no further than the Traeger Pro 780! This bad boy boasts 780 sq. in. of cooking space, WiFi connectivity through the WiFire app, and TurboTemp technology for lightning-fast, consistent heating. Whether you're into smoking, roasting, or baking, this grill has got you covered.
6. **Blackstone** - Last but certainly not least, we have the Blackstone 17\" Tabletop Griddle. This beast of a griddle delivers 12,000 BTUs thanks to its H-style burner, ensuring even heat distribution across its massive cooking surface (17 inches x 24 inches). Portable enough to take to the next tailgate or campsite, this griddle also sports a handy hood and Rear Grease Management System for simple cleanups.

There you have it, my friend! These six options cover all bases, offering something unique and exciting for each type of griller. So go ahead, give one of these babies a try – your taste buds will thank you!</s>

